---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import PayPalHero from '../../components/animated/PayPalHero';
---

<Site
	title="PayPal: Becoming the Default at Checkout · Steven Vanden Heuvel"
	description="On PayPal's Merchant Enablement team, I helped make PayPal more prominent and more consistent at checkout for top merchants, on weekly sprint cycles."
>
	<section class="cs-hero">
		<div class="cs-hero__inner">
			<a class="cs-back-top" href="/#work">← Case studies</a>
			<p class="eyebrow">Case study</p>
			<h1 class="cs-hero__title display">PayPal: Becoming the Default at Checkout</h1>
			<p class="cs-hero__lede">We needed to feature PayPal as the option the consumer wanted to use, and convert the transaction for the merchant.</p>
			<dl class="cs-meta">
				<div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Principal Designer · PayPal</dd></div>
				<div><dt>Team</dt><dd>Merchant Enablement</dd></div>
			</dl>
			<p class="cs-note">This work is proprietary to PayPal. Flows are shown generically and in person only, so they are not reproduced here.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="section__inner cs-orbit" data-animate="fade">
			<p class="eyebrow">The stage</p>
			<h2 class="cs-h2 display">PayPal partners with the top 100 merchants. The job was the checkout in front of them.</h2>
			<div class="cs-orbit__art">
				<PayPalHero client:load />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="section__inner cs-body" data-animate="fade">
			<div class="cs-block">
				<p class="eyebrow">What was unclear</p>
				<p class="cs-block__lede">PayPal showed up differently at every checkout.</p>
				<p>Each merchant integration carried its own patterns. Across vaulting, express, and standard flows, the experience changed from one surface to the next: app switch versus web, first time versus returning. That inconsistency worked against PayPal's top priority, greater checkout prominence to grow TPV.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="section__inner cs-body" data-animate="fade">
			<div class="cs-block">
				<p class="eyebrow">What I clarified</p>
				<p class="cs-block__lede">One proposal per merchant, on a weekly sprint.</p>
				<p>On the Merchant Enablement team I produced a proposal package for each merchant. Each one mapped the current checkout against a clearer target state across the four entry contexts, Wallet, Express, Standard first time, and Standard return, and the major variants: app switch versus web, Pay Later versus Pay in Full, passkey, and vaulting.</p>
				<p>Every package was the same stack: a screen audit, the complete checkout flows, a working prototype, a prototype video, and the decks for the merchant conversation.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="section__inner cs-body" data-animate="fade">
			<div class="cs-block">
				<p class="eyebrow">Who I influenced</p>
				<p class="cs-block__lede">The package was what the team took into the room.</p>
				<p>PMs and design leads used it in merchant conversations. I worked from PM briefs, with Principal Designer review and peer review inside a senior team. The proposals fed the merchant pitch for brands including Home Depot, Nintendo, Target, Best Buy, TikTok Shop, Chewy, and Microsoft.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="checkout-dead-end" class="section section--alt">
		<div class="section__inner cs-body" data-animate="fade">
			<div class="cs-block">
				<p class="eyebrow">The consumer side</p>
				<p class="cs-block__lede">The checkout dead end</p>
				<p>A customer reaches checkout and finds there is no card that can pay. The card expired, or it was declined, or it was removed, or it was never added in the first place. The order stops there.</p>
				<p>I built the Figma board that mapped that dead end back to every earlier moment the customer could have fixed the card. The board traced the touchpoints across roughly a month before checkout, marked which ones send a message today and which ones send nothing, and ended on the checkout experience itself.</p>
				<p>The structure came together fast because I used Claude Code to turn a Design Director's diagram into the underlying framework of the board, then designed into it. The screens came from teams across the company, which meant tracking down owners in parts of the organization I had not worked with before. The work was presented to senior leadership, and the board became the template the team now uses to map the next flows.</p>
				<p class="cs-caption">PayPal, 2026. Figma, Claude Code, cross-team research.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="section__inner cs-body" data-animate="fade">
			<div class="cs-block">
				<p class="eyebrow">What changed</p>
				<p class="cs-block__lede">Twenty-plus packages in my first six months, and the tooling to hold the pace.</p>
				<p>The tooling was not part of my assignment. To hold the weekly pace, I built a browser brief form and a Figma plugin on my own initiative. A merchant needs a full set of checkout flows, and building that set by hand took most of a day. With the plugin it takes 10 to 15 minutes, across the 38-merchant program. The work ties back to the TPV priority: make PayPal more prominent and more consistent at the point of payment.</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="cs-stats">
				<li><strong>20+</strong><span>Proposal packages shipped</span></li>
				<li><strong>15 min</strong><span>Per merchant, from most of a day</span></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section--alt">
		<div class="section__inner cs-back">
			<a class="btn" href="/#work">← All case studies</a>
			<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/work/plate">Next: Plate →</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Site>

<style>
	.cs-hero { max-width: var(--max); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-2xl) var(--gutter); }
	.cs-back-top { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); color: var(--text-mute); font-size: var(--text-body-sm); }
	.cs-back-top:hover { color: var(--lime); }
	.cs-hero__title { margin: var(--space-xs) 0 var(--space-lg); max-width: 20ch; }
	.cs-hero__lede { font-size: var(--text-deck); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.5; max-width: 56ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl); font-weight: 500; }
	.cs-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-md); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-lg) 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.cs-meta div { margin: 0; }
	.cs-meta dt { font-size: var(--text-label); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); }
	.cs-meta dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: var(--text-body); font-weight: 500; }
	.cs-note { margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0; padding: var(--space-md); border-left: 2px solid var(--lime); font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-mute); max-width: 64ch; }

	.cs-orbit { display: grid; gap: var(--space-md); }
	.cs-orbit__art { margin-top: var(--space-md); }
	.cs-h2 { max-width: 22ch; margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm); }

	.cs-body { display: grid; gap: var(--space-2xl); max-width: var(--max-narrow); }
	/* Hierarchy: eyebrow + subhead group as the headline, body is support. */
	.cs-block .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); }
	/* case-study eyebrows: nickel, normal weight, .03em, black */
	.eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-variation-settings: "wght" 400, "slnt" 0, "ital" 0; font-synthesis: none; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
	.cs-block__lede { color: var(--text); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 32px); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg); letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.25; }
	.cs-block p { color: #5A6565; margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; }
	.cs-block p + p { margin-top: var(--space-sm); }
	.cs-block .cs-caption { margin-top: var(--space-md); color: var(--text-mute); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }

	.cs-stats { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-md); }
	.cs-stats li { padding: var(--space-lg) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.cs-stats strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 900; font-style: normal; font-variation-settings: "wght" 900, "slnt" 0, "ital" 0; font-synthesis: none; font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 72px); color: var(--text); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); }
	.cs-stats span { color: var(--text-mute); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }

	.cs-back { display: flex; gap: var(--space-sm); flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
	.cs-back .btn--primary { background: var(--text); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--text); }
	.cs-back .btn--primary:hover { background: var(--text); border-color: var(--text); color: var(--bg); box-shadow: none; }

	@media (max-width: 880px) {
		.cs-orbit__art {
			width: 100%;
			aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
			overflow: visible;
			margin-top: var(--space-md);
		}
		.cs-hero__title { font-size: clamp(32px, 9vw, 56px); }
	}

	@media (max-width: 700px) {
		.cs-meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
		.cs-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
	}
</style>
